1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,320
Your head is older than your feet.

2
00:00:03,325 --> 00:00:05,987
Einstein predicted that gravity slows time.

3
00:00:06,287 --> 00:00:09,135
The closer to Earth, the slower a clock ticks.

4
00:00:10,035 --> 00:00:14,298
In 2010, physicists lifted one of two atomic clocks

5
00:00:14,298 --> 00:00:16,235
just 33 centimetres.

6
00:00:17,135 --> 00:00:18,784
The higher one ran faster.

7
00:00:19,084 --> 00:00:20,987
Over a 79-year life,

8
00:00:20,987 --> 00:00:23,715
that's about 90 billionths of a second.

9
00:00:24,615 --> 00:00:27,595
In 2022, clocks caught the difference

10
00:00:27,595 --> 00:00:28,906
across 1 millimetre,

11
00:00:29,206 --> 00:00:30,755
the width of a pencil tip.

12
00:00:31,655 --> 00:00:33,857
Your head sits much higher than that.

13
00:00:34,157 --> 00:00:36,775
So it ages a tiny bit faster than your feet.

14
00:00:37,675 --> 00:00:39,374
Too small to feel, but real.

15
00:00:39,774 --> 00:00:41,655
And it is happening, right now.
